## 3. Validation checklist

Run these on the **Bastion**. If you want evidence for the README, create `mkdir -p ~/evidence` and pipe outputs through `tee -a ~/evidence/p02.txt`. Public fingerprints are fine to record. **Never record passphrases or private keys.**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `apt list --upgradable 2>/dev/null \| tail -n +2` | Empty (fully patched) |
| 2 | `git --version; gpg --version \| head -1; ssh -V` | All three print versions |
| 3 | `systemctl is-enabled unattended-upgrades` | `enabled` |
| 4 | `getent hosts target` | `10.10.10.20 target` |
| 5 | `stat -c '%a %n' ~/.ssh ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab.pub ~/.ssh/config` | `700`, `600`, `644`, `600` |
| 6 | `ssh-keygen -lf ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab.pub` | `256 SHA256:... labadmin@bastion-lab (ED25519)` |
| 7 | `ssh-keygen -y -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab` | **Prompts for a passphrase** (proves it is protected). Press Ctrl+C to cancel. |
| 8 | `gpg --list-secret-keys --keyid-format=long` | `sec ed25519 ... [SC] [expires: ...]` and `ssb cv25519 ... [E]` |
| 9 | `echo "lab test" \| gpg --clearsign \| gpg --verify` | `Good signature from "Your Name <...>"` |
| 10 | `ls ~/.gnupg/openpgp-revocs.d/` | One `.rev` file |
| 11 | `ssh-add -l` | Lists your ed25519 key (agent running) |
| 12 | `timedatectl \| grep -E 'synchronized\|NTP'` | `System clock synchronized: yes` |
| 13 | `ss -tlnp` | **Still no listener on port 22** |
| 14 | `ls ~/.ssh` and `ls ~/.gnupg` | No stray or unexpected files |

**Troubleshooting:**
- `gpg: signing failed: Inappropriate ioctl for device` → run `export GPG_TTY=$(tty)` again.
- `Permissions ... are too open` from ssh → re-run the `chmod` commands from Step D.

